WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.301
Yang Guifei stood in the splendid palace garden.

00:00:03.651 --> 00:00:05.902
What she loved to eat most was fresh lychees.

00:00:06.252 --> 00:00:11.055
So that she could eat lychees, the emperor ordered fast horses to deliver lychees into the palace.

00:00:11.405 --> 00:00:14.561
As soon as the sky brightened, the riders mounted their fine horses and set off.

00:00:14.911 --> 00:00:19.982
The fine horses galloped, crossing high mountains and leaping over great rivers.

00:00:20.332 --> 00:00:24.263
Red dust rolled as the basket was passed on, station after station.

00:00:24.613 --> 00:00:27.881
Facing the wind, the riders raced on at flying speed.

00:00:28.231 --> 00:00:31.195
At every station, a new rider took over the relay.

00:00:31.545 --> 00:00:34.994
The basket full of lychees did not stop for a single moment.

00:00:35.344 --> 00:00:39.319
At last, the fresh lychees were delivered into the palace.

00:00:39.669 --> 00:00:43.826
The palace maids carefully carried the fruit basket and presented it to the consort.

00:00:44.176 --> 00:00:47.595
The consort was already waiting in the hall, looking forward to this gift.

00:00:47.945 --> 00:00:54.825
Yang Guifei peeled a lychee, took a taste, and broke into a happy smile.

00:00:55.175 --> 00:01:01.461
Later, the poet Du Mu wrote 'a rider in the red dust, and the consort smiles' — and so this story was handed down.

